<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy details lira min/max rates in ERM.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy details lira min/max rates in ERM.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lira's minimum intervention rate in Europe's exchange rate mechanism against the mark is 852.59 lire per mark and the maximum rate is 1,149.56 per mark, the Bank of Italy said.</p>
<p>The lira's central parity against the mark is 990.004, as announced late on Sunday in Brussels.  </p>
<p>Following is a table of the lira's new maximum, minimum and central rates against other currencies in the grid.</p>
<p>			   Minimum	  Central	  Maximum</p>
<p> Belgian franc	 41.336	   47.9991	  55.736</p>
<p> Danish crown	  223.51	   259.542	  301.38</p>
<p> German mark	   852.59	   990.004	  1149.56</p>
<p> Spanish peseta	10.022	   11.6372	  13.513</p>
<p> French franc	  254.21	   295.183	  342.76</p>
<p> Irish pound	   2055.61	  2386.95	  2771.70</p>
<p> Dutch guilder	 756.68	   878.647	  1020.27</p>
<p> Austrian schilling  121.18	   140.715	  163.39</p>
<p> Portuguese escudo   8.317	    9.65805	  11.215</p>
<p> Finnish markka	280.45	   325.658	  378.16</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
